A powerful normal in Mr. Karate’s arsenal, great for pushing your advantage at close range. Its link to 2C on hit gives you reliable light-to-heavy combo routes, and on block, this same sequence shuts down reversal lights and throws from your opponent. 
}}

====Close C====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=
|moveId=mrkarate_clC
|input=
|description=* The faster of Mr. Karate’s close heavies but has short proximity detection
* A feint cancel lets this move link to 2C and gives Mr. Karate massive reward on Counter Hit, and makes this move his most advantageous normal on block
* Fantastic on both hit and block if feint cancelled, otherwise very punishable
This gut punch is a great close-range button… as long as you remember to feint cancel it. Even though it’s a frame slower than 2C, it links to said button on normal hit when you feint cancel it, and on block that same feint cancel is plus enough to allow a follow-up close/far B or 2C to beat any reversal normals from your opponent. 
Counter Hitting with this normal gives you a triple-heavy combo, maximizing your damage. To do this, microdash after the first close C, then do a close C/D > feint cancel > 2C > special. It’s tough to time, but you can use your Rev button’s dash macro here.
}}

====Close D====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=
|moveId=mrkarate_clD
|input=
|description=* Hits twice, but only the second hit cancels, easily letting you confirm hit or block but potentially leaving you vulnerable to Guard Cancels
* Forces stand on hit, like all close D’s
* Links to 2C on normal hit when feint cancelled
This here’s your main combo starter. Landing it should be one of your goals as Mr. Karate, because from there you easily get this character’s big combos. Like with close C, you can feint cancel it on block and it will be plus, but unlike close C, the opponent can trade their way out of most follow-up pressure (unless you frame trap them with something like charged DP brake).
}}

