|description2= Mr. Karate lifts one leg up and enters his Drago Supremo stance. He has four different followups out of this stance, but when used by itself Drago Supremo functions as a parry that works on strikes and projectiles, with different properties depending on how soon after activating the stance Mr. Karate parries an attack. Drago Supremo has a bit of startup similar to Nightmare Geese's counters, 3 frames for the normal version and 2 frames for the REV version, so it will not work as a wakeup reversal against properly timed meaties.

Drago Supremo will parry all Mid and High strike including supers and REV Blows as well as non-REV and non-super projectiles, but loses to Lows and Throws. Additionally Drago Supremo cannot counter attacks that are behind Mr. Karate such as cross-ups. When a parryable strike connects, Mr. Karate will automatically follow up with Dragon Roar. When a parryable projectile connects, Mr. Karate will destroy it and remain in Drago Supremo stance.

* '''REV Drago Supremo''' and its followups are mostly the same, but Mr. Karate gains the ability to Dragon Burst after '''Shouran Kyaku''' and can REV Accel after '''Dragon Roar''' and '''Dragon Howl'''. Mr. Karate also gains the ability to parry Lows and REV projectiles, though the stance will still lose to Throws, cross-ups, and super projectiles.

* If Mr. Karate parries a strike immediately after activating Drago Supremo, he will instead perform '''Dragon Howl''', a stronger attack. Even if the opponent was airborne when they triggered Dragon Howl, they will be forced into a grounded state for the animation. '''REV Dragon Howl''' can be followed up with Dragon Burst or a REV Accel. This makes Drago Supremo a good option when attempting a Guard Cancel, as certain REV Accel blockstrings that blow up other Guard Cancel options like a REV Accel into a REV DP will be countered by Dragon Howl.

* If Mr. Karate parries a projectile immediately after activating Drago Supremo, he will reflect the projectile instead of destroying it.
